meta {
  name: Assign Row
  type: http
  seq: 27
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/runs/{{reconRunId}}/rows/{{reconAssignRowId}}/assignment
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "userId": "{{currentUserId}}",
    "note": "Enter the deal from the Dash line"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("the row is with the producer, from the owner", function () {
    const assignment = res.getBody().assignment;
    expect(assignment.user.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("currentUserId"));
    expect(assignment.user.name).to.be.a("string");
    expect(assignment.assignedBy.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("reconOwnerId"));
    expect(assignment.assignedAt).to.be.a("string");
    expect(assignment.note).to.equal("Enter the deal from the Dash line");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /carrier-reconciliation/runs/:id/rows/:rowId/assignment — hand a row to someone

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation`
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:write`

  Assigns a row to one of the agency's **active Producers or CSRs** (the
  `Get Options` pool), changes the note on it, or takes it back. The
  assignee is notified in-app and by push — type
  `reconciliation.row_assigned`, "Dash policy assigned to you",
  `<policy no> · <customer> · <tab>`, opening
  `/reconciliation/assigned?row=<id>` — and the row appears on their
  `List Assigned Rows`. No email (owner, 26 Oct 2026).

  - Only a row **still waiting on a decision** (`needsReview`, review
    `open`), on a finished run nobody re-uploaded, can be assigned. Taking a
    row back always works.
  - A row **missing from the app** goes only to someone who can book a sale
    — `canRecordSale` on `Get Options` (`leads:write` + `deal_audits:write`,
    by effective permission, never role name). Anyone else is a `400`
    `RECONCILIATION_ASSIGNEE_CANNOT_SELL` (PAC-173 PR 4, owner 28 Oct 2026):
    the assignee records it as Sold or a Cancel rewrite by entering the lead
    and the sale. A standard CSR still takes rows in every other tab.
  - A **1-800 policy the app does not have** (1-800 review, `dash_only`) goes
    only to someone who can set it up for service — `canSetUpService`
    (`leads:write`, which every default Producer and CSR holds). Anyone else
    is a `400` `RECONCILIATION_ASSIGNEE_CANNOT_SERVICE` (PAC-173 PR 5). A
    1-800 policy the app already has takes Other only, so anyone may.
  - Handing the row to someone else, or taking it back, **clears an outcome
    under way** in the same write: the new person starts over, because the
    first one's lead stays in their own pipeline. A note change for the same
    person keeps it; a finished outcome is kept either way.
  - The same person again only changes the note: no new notification.
  - Nobody is notified when the owner assigns a row to themselves, or on an
    unassign.
  - The assignment is its own field, so saving a decision (`Review Row`)
    never drops it. A decided row keeps its assignee as the record of who
    worked it, but leaves their list.
  - A re-upload of the same period carries the assignment to a row that
    still says the same thing (same key, match and issues), without
    notifying again. Removing or transferring the person releases or moves
    their open rows (see `Users/Transfer Work`, `Users/Deactivate User`).

  ## Body
  - `userId` — the assignee's id, or `null` to unassign
  - `note` — optional, ≤ 1000 characters; omitted keeps the note when the
    assignee is unchanged

  ## Response `200` — the `ReconciliationRowView`, with
  `assignment: { user: {id, name}, assignedBy: {id, name}, assignedAt, note }`

  ## Errors
  - `400` — not an active Producer or CSR of this agency; validation
  - `400` `RECONCILIATION_ASSIGNEE_CANNOT_SELL` — a row missing from the app,
    to someone who cannot book a sale (checked only for a new assignee)
  - `400` `RECONCILIATION_ASSIGNEE_CANNOT_SERVICE` — a 1-800 row the app does
    not have, to someone who cannot set it up for service (new assignee only)
  - `404` — no such run or row in the agency
  - `409` — the row is already decided or needs no decision; the run was
    replaced by a newer upload or did not finish; someone else changed the
    assignment, or the assignee's outcome, at the same moment
}
